      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "> That was my rough idea that ~1% of bumpfee calls would be for silent payments once the feature is merged.\n>     Actually, I think it would be the main pain point of integrating this: forcing almost everyone to add an argument they don't use, just because the node can't know if an external transaction contains silent payments?\n\nMost users shouldn't have the same descriptors loaded in multiple wallets; the only valid setups I can think of are offline signer/online watch-only wallet pairs. I expect most wallets to have few external transactions, but I could be wrong. \n\n> Also, I was actually expecting the bumpfee could only be used for silent payments if the tx is paid by a wallet known by the node receiving the rpc request? But maybe the SP instructions can transmit the new S value or something like that without making the sender's private keys computable by another node?\n\nI'm a bit confused here. SP txs are like regular txs and can be fee-bumped in the usual way. The idea here is to prevent users from accidentally burning UTXOs.\n\n> Yes, i was thinking about making this one mandatory, which seems clearer than having a 'force' argument that has to be here for all non-silent payment txs without having a name giving context what it is for\n\nI think it might be weirder to have a mandatory `sp_info` argument. It is less weird if it is only mandatory for external transactions as opposed to all transactions. Maybe this is what you meant? I can see how just having `sp_info` and requiring it for external transactions can be better than requiring `force=True` with the optional `sp_info`.",
