      "body": "> 5\\. I'm a bit confused here. SP txs are like regular txs and can be fee-bumped in the usual way. The idea here is to prevent users from accidentally burning UTXOs.\n\nI just mean, in the case SP outputs have to be recomputed by the node receiving the feebump RPC (because as said in the issue description, inputs would change), either the node has to have a wallet knowing the private keys of the wallet owning the utxos being spent, or SP instructions have to provide a way to recompute the new SP outputs, but without giving enough info to be able to recompute the sender's private key.\n\nMaybe you already accounted for this and there is no problem.",
