      "created_at": "2026-11-04T15:45:48Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-04T15:45:48Z",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "The only thing I could find is that Cake Wallet disables speeding up silent payments. But that means they are talking about 'internal' ones they know the destination sp address of.\n\nI'm wondering if a 'less tricky' thing would be to start by  reviving the issues like https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/20935, which already had some PR started :https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/25776\nSo when calling bumpfee, user could still at least fee bump silent payments until the current change output allows, by just adding an option 'do not add inputs'\n\nOf course in this case (blindly bumping without recalculating SP outputs), we would also have to make sure other things that could break the SP outputs don't occur, like guaranteeing outputs keep the same order",
